course: dictionary
lesson: 13012
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it. The word extraction is a good example. «The dentist planned a tooth extraction.» The clues are dentist and tooth, so extraction means taking a tooth out of a mouth.
explain: «The factory uses extraction to get salt from sea water.» Now the clues are factory, salt and sea water, so extraction means getting a substance out of a mixture. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «She is of Irish extraction, so her grandad was born in Ireland.» Here extraction does not mean pulling anything out. It means the country or family a person comes from. This meaning is formal, so you will meet it more in writing than in everyday talk.
fact: Extraction means taking or pulling something out.
fact: In science, extraction means getting a substance out of a mixture, such as salt from sea water or juice from fruit.
fact: At the dentist, a tooth extraction means taking out a tooth.
fact: «Oil extraction» and «metal extraction» mean taking oil or metal out of the ground or out of rock.
fact: «Of Irish extraction» means the person comes from an Irish family or country.
exercise: «The dentist carried out a tooth extraction.» What was taken out? | A bicycle | A song | *A tooth
exercise: «Salt was made by extraction from sea water.» What does extraction mean here? | Swimming across the sea | *Getting salt out of the water | Pulling a fish out of the sea | Making the sea colder
exercise: «She is of French extraction.» Which word means the family or country she comes from? | *extraction | French | She | is
test: «Oil extraction takes place deep under the ground.» What is oil extraction? | Washing oil off a car | Painting a picture with oil | *Taking oil out of the ground | Heating a pan with oil
test: «Metals are got from rock by extraction in a factory.» Which meaning is used? | Family or country of origin | A kind of music | Pulling a tooth out | *Getting a substance out of a mixture
exam: Priya reads «He is of Polish extraction.» What does extraction mean? | *The country or family he comes from | Getting juice from fruit | Pulling something out | A school lesson
